## Angular workspace boundary

- This is an Angular 22 standalone, strict, zoneless workspace using the 2025 filename style.
- The Angular workspace root is `{frontend.root}`. It must not contain a root `src/` application.
- Applications are ordered as `{angular.applicationNames}` and live only under `{frontend.appsRoot}/<application>/`.
- Reusable Angular libraries are ordered as `{angular.libraryNames}` and live only under `{frontend.libsRoot}/<library>/`.
- Keep application features and platform adapters inside their owning application. Move code into a library only when it has a real reusable package boundary.
- Keep shared UI and framework-neutral utilities in libraries; do not make one application import another application's source.
- Treat generated artifacts and `dist/` as outputs, never source ownership.
- The frontend `package.json`, `angular.json`, and TypeScript configurations are assembled configuration boundaries. Add stack-specific fields through their owning puzzle pieces.
- Routing is `{angular.routingMode}`, SSR is `{angular.ssr}`, and component styles use `{angular.styleMode}`.
- No test runner is selected here. Test framework and placement behavior belong to separate capabilities.
